    "body": "So, after digging into this, we should most likely keep the check, and change the comparison from `current session history entry` to `displayedEntry` in step 12.7, because the semantic intent of this algorithm basically boils down to:\n\n1. If the entries are different, it means we are navigating \"somewhere else\" -> fire the navigate event\nwhere as the current state of the spec says:\n1. Something must have raced and changed `current session history entry` (since it's on the session history traversal queue) in order for \"fire the navigate event\" to happen, which is a very nonsensical thing to spec.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
