    "updated_at": "2026-09-09T15:40:39Z",
    "body": "> > This is always false. I am unsure if it is okay to remove it, or if this is comparing against the wrong thing\n> \n> This is technically not true, because `current session history entry` is mutated on the SHTQ, where as these steps are queued in a global task (so run on the event loop), so actually `current session history entry` can mutate in between all of the steps in 12.N-M, which is another reason why I think `displayedEntry` is the correct thing to compare against (as `active session history entry` only mutates on the event loop)\n\nHmm I didnt really think about that, I suppose that might be technically true by spec wording, but I can't (perhaps wrongly!) imagine a way how this would be implemented in that way in reality, and it kind of makes me shudder to think about considering such cases given the amount of races already W.R.T task ordering. Makes me wonder the spec model around the SHTQ needs to be formalised a bit more about this type of assumption, but I suppose that's a different topic altogether",
