    "created_at": "2026-09-09T18:14:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-09T18:14:45Z",
    "body": "> Hmm I didnt really think about that, I suppose that might be technically true by spec wording, but I can't (perhaps wrongly!) imagine a way how this would be implemented in that way in reality, and it kind of makes me shudder to think about considering such cases given the amount of races already W.R.T task ordering. Makes me wonder the spec model around the SHTQ needs to be formalised a bit more about this type of assumption, but I suppose that's a different topic altogether\n\nThe SHTQ and event loop [are parallel](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#tn-session-history-traversal-queue). We have [current session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#nav-current-history-entry) that can only be mutated on the SHTQ and the [active session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#nav-active-history-entry) which can only be mutated on the event loop, and given that these steps run on the event loop (queued global task in step 12), at any time in these steps, in parallel [current session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#nav-current-history-entry) can mutate. I this is the biggest explanation for why the spec must be worded wrong, because its nonsensical to rely on a data race effectively (`targetEntry` having to change in parallel between the steps 12.2 to 12.7), to fire a navigate event.",
