    "updated_at": "2026-09-09T19:15:28Z",
    "body": "I agree with all that, will try change and figure out the relevant tests.\n\nTo be clear, I was mostly musing that in real implementations this wouldnt be a race at all, it's deterministically false, whereas in the spec it is one. Given how much of apply the history step is already about task ordering, I was more wondering about the SHTQ being given slightly more restrictive model than plain \"in parallel\" to make it simpler to trace",
